"hero": "<section class=\"page-hero\"><div class=\"shell\">{{ppp:breadcrumbs}}<span class=\"eyebrow\">Company updates</span><h1>Ellis Services Group news and updates</h1><p>Practical notes about sending clear property maintenance enquiries.</p></div></section>" as TrustedHtml,
"sections": [
{
"id": "section-1",
"kind": "faq",
"container": "<section class=\"section\"><div class=\"shell cards\"><article class=\"card\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">Company update</span><h3>A clearer way to send a property maintenance enquiry</h3><p>Keep the address, problem, access and approval information in one place.</p><a href=\"news-clearer-property-maintenance-enquiry.html\">Read update →</a></article><article class=\"card\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">Company update</span><h3>What makes a useful plumbing or electrical work order</h3><p>Use observable facts rather than an assumed diagnosis.</p><a href=\"news-useful-property-work-order.html\">Read update →</a></article><article class=\"card\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">Company update</span><h3>Keeping access information with the repair request</h3><p>Help avoid back-and-forth when a property needs attention.</p><a href=\"news-keeping-access-information-together.html\">Read update →</a></article></div><!-- site-intent:start --><div class=\"intent-content shell text-column\" data-site-intent><h2>Choose a practical booking note</h2><p>The enquiry note covers the first description. The work-order note records assessable tasks and approval limits. The access note keeps the visit arrangements current and private. For fault-specific explanations, use the insights guides instead; these company notes do not replace a technical inspection.</p><ul class=\"intent-links\"><li><a href=\"news-clearer-property-maintenance-enquiry.html\">Prepare the initial maintenance enquiry</a></li><li><a href=\"news-useful-property-work-order.html\">Define the work-order scope</a></li><li><a href=\"news-keeping-access-information-together.html\">Keep repair access information together</a></li></ul><details><summary>{{ppp:faq:0:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:0:answer}}</details></div><!-- site-intent:end --></section>" as TrustedHtml,
"items": [
{
"question": "Which note should a property manager start with?",
"answer": "<p>Start with the enquiry note when the fault is first reported. Use the work-order note when turning that report into an instruction, then the access note to confirm how the agreed visit will take place.</p>" as TrustedHtml
}
]
},
{
"id": "section-2",
"kind": "rich",
"html": "<section class=\"section\" data-content-hub><div class=\"shell text-column\"><h2>From a repair request to a clear work order</h2><p>These practical company notes explain how to describe a job, coordinate entry and record approval. Each note covers a different part of the booking process so owners and managers can keep the same property reference from first contact through to the agreed work.</p><h3>Start with the condition at the property</h3><p>Use the initial-enquiry note for the location, affected room and current symptom. Separate a reported fault from an improvement you want quoted, such as a new outlet or appliance connection. For the work itself, our <a href=\"plumbing.html\">plumbing service overview</a> and <a href=\"electrical.html\">electrical service overview</a> link to the relevant repair and installation pages.</p><h3>Keep access and approval distinct</h3><p>The access note covers entry to the property and equipment, the on-site contact and changed arrangements. The work-order note covers the requested tasks, decision-maker and approval boundaries. An occupant who provides access may not be authorised to approve additional repair costs. Keep private entry codes and keys out of public photos and pages.</p><p>For technical observations, use our <a href=\"insights.html\">plumbing and electrical guides</a>. For a rental, strata or other managed premises, see <a href=\"property-management.html\">property management maintenance</a>. When ready, <a href=\"contact.html\">send the request</a> with the address, current issue and contact details. The written quote confirms the property-specific work; a preparation checklist is not a diagnosis or a fixed-price package.</p></div></section>" as TrustedHtml
}
],
